# TypeScript

- Strict TypeScript. Exported functions and props have explicit types.
- No `any`, no `as any`, and no non-null assertion used to hide a missing check.
- No comments. The name carries the meaning.
- Colocate `*.test.ts` or `*.test.tsx` with the module it covers.
- Keep components free of network calls. Pass data in and events out.

```tsx
type PlaceholderProps = {
  title: string;
};

export function Placeholder({ title }: PlaceholderProps) {
  return <Text>{title}</Text>;
}
```
